    "description": "Voltage-drop reference for uncoated copper conductors in Steel Conduit. R and X are NEC Chapter 9 Table 9 values for 600 V cables, 3-phase, 60 Hz, 75 C, three single conductors in conduit. Effective impedance is calculated at PF 0.70 through 1.00 in 0.05 increments using Ze = R × PF + X × sqrt(1 - PF^2)."
